'use strict';
/* ============================================================================
   shipmodel.js — the player's starship, baked from a glTF asset.

   Embedded as base64 rather than fetched: fetch is blocked under file://, and
   the game is meant to run by opening index.html directly.

   The source rig animates a bone hierarchy, but the meshes carry no joint
   weights — each part is rigidly parented to one bone.  So rather than ship a
   skeleton and an animation evaluator, the bake samples the hierarchy at 24 Hz
   and stores a plain translation/rotation/scale per part per frame.  The
   runtime just interpolates between two frames.

   Vertex data is quantised: positions to int16 against each part's own
   bounding box, normals to int8, UVs to uint16 against their own range.  That
   is what keeps a 137k-triangle ship inside a few megabytes of JavaScript.
   ============================================================================ */

